{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2019-12-13 02:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E FILES AMENDED PLAN OF REORGANIZATION', 'text': "PG&E FILES AMENDED PLAN OF REORGANIZATION; REMAINS ON TRACK TO ACHIEVE CONFIRMATION OF PLAN BEFORE JUNE 30 DEADLINE.COMPANY HAS SETTLED ALL MAJOR WILDFIRE CLAIMS AND RESOLVED DISPUTED RELEASE PROVISIONS BETWEEN WILDFIRE VICTIMS AND INSURANCE COMPANIES.CO TODAY FILED AN AMENDED PLAN OF REORGANIZATION WITH BANKRUPTCY COURT IN ITS CHAPTER 11 CASES.WORKING WITH STAKEHOLDERS TO CONFIRM SUPPORT FOR PLAN, TO OBTAINING REGULATORY APPROVAL FROM CALIFORNIA PUBLIC UTILITIES COMMISSION.WORKING TO ACHIEVING CONFIRMATION OF PLAN BY BANKRUPTCY COURT IN ADVANCE OF JUNE 30, 2020.PG&E'S PLAN IS FULLY FINANCEABLE THROUGHOUT CAPITAL STRUCTURE.PG&E'S PLAN WOULD ACCOMPLISH PAYING $1 BILLION IN FULL SETTLEMENT OF CLAIMS OF CERTAIN PUBLIC ENTITIES LIKE CITIES, COUNTIES RELATING TO WILDFIRES.PLAN WOULD ACCOMPLISH COMPENSATING INSURANCE SUBROGATION CLAIMANTS FROM TRUST FUNDED FOR THEIR BENEFIT IN AMOUNT OF $11 BILLION."}